            "text": "Page 1\n\nINSTALLATION NOTES:\n1. This drawing assumes a level deck unless otherwise stated. BAUDER tapered systems are designed for installation on level decks.\n\n2. BAUDER LTD recommend that this scheme should be installed starting from the thickest boards, so that in the event of discrepancies in roof size, the flatboard areas can be modified accordingly.\n\n3. Boards to be close butted and staggered. Upstands to perimeters, rooflights, tank houses etc, to be raised where necessary to incorporate the thickness of the insulation.\n\n4. Mitre Boards are available in all falls. They are denoted on this plan by an \"R\" or a \"V\" to signify Ridge and Valley. The corner of the board marked \"R\" or \"V\" is where the high point of the board should be located.\n\n5. Please note that all offcuts of tapered insulation boards should be used within the scheme. These are not deemed as waste boards by Bauder.\n\nNOTES:\nAlthough this tapered insulation scheme is designed to help shed water from the roof, we cannot guarantee that ponding will be totally eliminated.\n\nPlease note that ponding water may occur around the flatboard gutter area due to a lack of cross falls. However this is not detrimental to the Bauder system\n\nDrainage/Outlet Locations TBC\nRoof Extents TBC\n\nKey:\n= 100mm BauderPIR FA-TE Flatboard - NO Baselayer\n= 60mm BauderPIR FA-TE Flatboard - NO Baselayer\n= Suitable Insulation Infill\n= Tapered Insulation\n---- = Valleys to be cut on site\n\nNOTE:\nALL roof dimensions, rooflights and outlet\npositions to be checked BEFORE the\nTapered scheme is ordered.\no = Outlet\n-> = Direction of Falls in Tapered Insulation\n\nPlan Details:\nNB1 Staircore Roof\nNB1 Roof A\nNB1 Roof B\n200mm Flat Board (Not Included In Thermal Calculation)\n\nNB2 Staircore Roof\nNB2 Roof A\nNB2 Roof B\n200mm Flat Board (Not Included In Thermal Calculation)\n\nMaterial: BauderPIR FA G16\nMulti Layered Tapered Build Up Section - 1 in 60\n(Not To Scale)\n160 mm BauderPIR FA G16 Baselayer\n3: 70 mm\n4: 90 mm\n5: 110 mm\n6: 130 mm\n7: 150 mm\n8: 170 mm\n1: 190 mm\n2: 210 mm\n3: 230 mm\n4: 250 mm\n5: 270 mm\n6: 290 mm\n310 mm\n\nNOTE REGARDING U-VALUES\nThe individual roof areas achieve the 'U' Values stated in the table. These U-Values are calculated according to BS EN ISO 6946:2017(E) Annex 'E' and do not take into account materials below the deck, significant point thermal bridges or linear transmittance unless specified otherwise. Refer to separate Bauder U-Value Calculation and Condensation Risk analysis where available for the complete system build-up and achieved U-Value.\n\nRoof Name Area: NB2 Roof A (Gutter)\nDeck Type: Bauder - Concrete\nMinimum U Value: 0.35 W/m² K\nEffective U Value: 0.14 W/m² K\nApproximate Net Roof Area (m²): 105.16\nApproximate Area of Insulation to be Bonded (m²): 123.65\nTotal Insulation Required Inc Waste (m²): 137.52\n\nRoof Name Area: NB1 Roof A (Gutter)\nDeck Type: Bauder - Concrete\nMinimum U Value: 0.21 W/m² K\nEffective U Value: 0.14 W/m² K\nApproximate Net Roof Area (m²): 97.57\nApproximate Area of Insulation to be Bonded (m²): 110.87\nTotal Insulation Required Inc Waste (m²): 125.28\n\nRoof Name Area: NB2 Staircore Roof\nDeck Type: Bauder - Concrete\nMinimum U Value: 0.21 W/m² K\nEffective U Value: 0.11 W/m² K\nApproximate Net Roof Area (m²): 05.98\nApproximate Area of Insulation to be Bonded (m²): 12.30\nTotal Insulation Required Inc Waste (m²): 17.28\n\nRoof Name Area: NB1 Staircore Roof\nDeck Type: Bauder - Concrete\nMinimum U Value: 0.21 W/m² K\nEffective U Value: 0.12 W/m² K\nApproximate Net Roof Area (m²): 13.34\nApproximate Area of Insulation to be Bonded (m²): 21.33\nTotal Insulation Required Inc Waste (m²): 25.20\n\nRoof Name Area: NB2 Roof B\nDeck Type: Bauder - Concrete\nMinimum U Value: 0.21 W/m² K\nEffective U Value: 0.11 W/m² K\nApproximate Net Roof Area (m²): 411.42\nApproximate Area of Insulation to be Bonded (m²): 650.31\nTotal Insulation Required Inc Waste (m²): 699.84\n\nRoof Name Area: NB1 Roof B\nDeck Type: Bauder - Concrete\nMinimum U Value: 0.21 W/m² K\nEffective U Value: 0.11 W/m² K\nApproximate Net Roof Area (m²): 141.61\nApproximate Area of Insulation to be Bonded (m²): 232.80\nTotal Insulation Required Inc Waste (m²): 248.40\n\nImportant Notice:\nThis scheme is of a\nMULTI-LAYER Design and as\nsuch extra Insulation Adhesive\nwill be Required to Adhere the\nTaper Boards to the Base\nLayer/Overlay Layer.\n\nPRELIMINARY DESIGN - SUBJECT TO CHANGE\nTO BE USED FOR LAYOUT, INSULATION DEPTHS\nAND PRELIMINARY QUOTE INFORMATION ONLY.\nFINAL DESIGN TO BE CONFIRMED BY THE CLIENT PRIOR TO ORDER.\nShould this project be ordered, any amendments necessary that have\nadditional cost implications may be subject to further costs.\n\nRidge situation\nValley situation\n\nIMPORTANT NOTE:\nThe Bauder Upstand Insulation\nin accordance with the Bauder\nSpecification and is to be\nordered separately. This is Not\nincluded within the taper\nscheme and associated\nquotation.\n\nAll Dimensions, positions of Rooflights and Outlets\nare to be checked on site BEFORE the tapered\nscheme is ordered.\n\nRevisions:\nRev: B\nDate: 09/10/26\nNotes: Updated To New Issue Plan\nBy: MM\n\nRev: A\nDate: 12/05/26\nNotes: 200mm Flat Board Removed\nBy: BR\n\nRev: -\nDate: 08/05/26\nNotes: Drawing Issued For Approval & Comment\nBy: BR\n\nBAUDER\n\nUK OFFICE\nBauder Limited\n70 Landseer Road, Ipswich,\nSuffolk IP3 0DH,\nEngland.\nTel: +44 (0)1473 257671\nFax: +44 (0)1473 230761\nEmail: technical@bauder.co.uk\nbauder.co.uk\n\nIRELAND OFFICE\nBauder Limited\nO'Duffy Centre, Cross Lane,\nCarrickmacross, Co. Monaghan,\nIreland.\nTel: +353 (0)42 9692 333\nFax: +353 (0)42 9692 839\nEmail: technical@bauder.ie\nbauder.ie\n\nThis scheme design should be checked against all project related\ndrawings and site requirements. Bauder Ltd should be notified\nimmediately of any discrepancies.\n\nThe placement of an order for this scheme design confirms that you\nare not aware of any design changes to the roof area(s) concerned\nand approve the scheme as designed. Following this approval,\nshould any amendments be necessary or the installation deviates\nfrom the designed scheme, such changes may be subject to further\ncosts and time for replacements.\n\nContract Name: St Clare's School\n\nMULTI-LAYER BauderPIR FA G16 TAPER SCHEME\nContract No: B269681\nDrawing No: LTF-001\nRef No: D.S - 09074_26.03\nDesigned to Drawing No:\nScale: 1:300 @ ISO A3\nDrawn By: MM\nDate: 09/10/2026",
